[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/479229837","html_url":"https://github.com/xunit/xunit/issues/1916#issuecomment-479229837","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/1916","id":479229837,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3OTIyOTgzNw==","user":{"login":"bradwilson","id":16944,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16944?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson","html_url":"https://github.com/bradwilson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-04-02T22:17:54Z","updated_at":"2019-04-02T22:17:54Z","body":"Result from running with the .NET Framework console runner:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/16944/55439421-66ffc800-5559-11e9-91cc-79d94333f522.png)\r\n\r\nThe .NET Framework results are probably what you expected: one passes (T), one fails (U).\r\n\r\nResult from running with the .NET Core VSTest runner:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/16944/55439262-dde89100-5558-11e9-96c2-f420715c7403.png)\r\n\r\nThe VSTest results are probably not what you expected, because the argument serialization inherent in VSTest ended up with two identical unique IDs for T and U. While I sort of expected this result, it could be argued that it is a bug (that we might not be able to fix).\r\n\r\nThe specific R# runner behavior that you're showing as a bug is actually a bug in the R# runner, because it discovered tests it shouldn't be able to run. So there are two bugs here: one ours (the T and U versions have identical IDs), one Resharpers (it shows you tests it can't run).\r\n\r\nI will leave this bug open here in the even that maybe we can find/fix our issue, but the R# issue should be reported separately to the R# team.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/479229837/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bradwilson","id":16944,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16944?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson","html_url":"https://github.com/bradwilson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2248080732,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIyNDgwODA3MzI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/events/2248080732","actor":{"login":"bradwilson","id":16944,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16944?v=4","