/users/bradwilson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2019-04-02T22:18:09Z","label":{"name":"type: Bug","color":"fbca04"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/479260087","html_url":"https://github.com/xunit/xunit/issues/1916#issuecomment-479260087","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/1916","id":479260087,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3OTI2MDA4Nw==","user":{"login":"estrizhok","id":463971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Mzk3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/463971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok","html_url":"https://github.com/estrizhok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-04-02T23:51:54Z","updated_at":"2019-04-02T23:54:46Z","body":"I believe you incorrectly identified the root cause. Yes, the IDs are the same. (I actually did not check that, but it is a different problem, and it should not matter in this case. It might have been a single test case, thus having a unique id, the result would have still been the same). But whatever the IDs are, there are two test cases reported by the xUnit adapter, when an IDE executes a discovery for the project. Here I am talking about `dotnet vstest` and [DiscoveryRequestPayload](https://github.com/Microsoft/vstest/blob/master/src/Microsoft.TestPlatform.ObjectModel/Client/Payloads/DiscoveryRequestPayload.cs). \r\n\r\nHere comes an error.\r\n\r\nIf the IDE then tries to execute any of those test cases by specifying them explicitly in [TestRunRequestPayload.TestCases](https://github.com/Microsoft/vstest/blob/master/src/Microsoft.TestPlatform.ObjectModel/Client/Payloads/TestRunRequestPayload.cs), the xUnit adapter will fail to deserialize that test case (and abort execution completely, too, even if it is not the only test case in the run).\r\n\r\nIt is different from running tests using `dotnet test` command in your example, because (as I understand it) the latter discovers and runs in the same process at about the same moment in time, thus eliminating the need to deserialize test cases.\r\n\r\nI disagree that it is a bug of R#. All R# does is shows the test cases xUnit adapter reports. But when R# tries to feed the same test cases back to xUnit adapter, telling it to run them, the adapter crushes in deserialization. And it only those types of tests (ones with types of generic arguments passed as arguments) that are causing the problem. All others can be executed just fine.\r\n\r\nHope this helps.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/479260087/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"estrizhok","id":463971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Mzk3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/463971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok","html_url":"https://github.com/estrizhok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/estrizhok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api